<title>USA: U.S. Oct personal income unchanged.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct personal income unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Oct  Sept-Rev from  Aug-Rev from  July</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  UNCH   0.6    0.6    0.6    0.5   UNCH</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  UNCH   0.6    0.6    0.5    0.5   UNCH</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs     -0.3    0.4    0.4    0.5    0.4   -0.2</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.5    0.1    0.1    0.5    0.5    0.2</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.2   -0.1   -0.1    0.4    0.5    0.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Oct  Sept-Rev from  Aug-Rev from   July</p>
<p> Income		   6,544  6,542  6,542  6,501  6,501  6,462</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,662  5,659  5,661  5,627  5,627  5,597</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,367  5,339  5,339  5,337  5,335  5,313</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,202  5,175  5,175  5,172  5,172  5,148</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   629    627    634    643    643    625</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,557  1,552  1,547  1,543  1,540  1,544</p>
<p> -Services		3,017  2,996  2,994  2,987  2,988  2,979</p>
<p> Personal Saving	  295    320    323    290    292    284</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.2    5.7    5.7    5.2    5.2    5.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Oct  Sept-Rev from  Aug-Rev from   July</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,685  3,692  3,696  3,661  3,665  3,631</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   679    680    680    681    680    675</p>
<p> -Services		1,284  1,288  1,289  1,271  1,272  1,258</p>
<p> -Government		649    647    647    645    645    643</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    528    530    524    526    521    522</p>
<p> -Farm			 51     53     48     52     49     50</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  477    477    476    473    472    473</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected October personal income to be unchanged and spending to be up 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The department said private wage and salary disbursements decreased $8.9 billion in October as compared with a rise of $28.2 billion in September.</p>
